{
 "_notes": "Land-use preset buckets for the app's Preset filter. Each bucket is a list of 2-digit Florida DOR use-code categories (Fla. Admin. Code R. 12D-8.008; names in fetch_code_descriptions.py DOR_CATEGORIES). A parcel's category comes from features.dor_use_code (the statewide DOR roll, '001' = 01) and, where that is blank, from the county's own land_use_code via dor_codes.normalize_code. Buckets may overlap (vacant commercial is in both 'commercial' and 'vacant_land'). Category 80 is 'undefined/reserved' in the current rule but most counties still use it for vacant government land (avg ~50 acres per parcel), so it sits with government. Category counts were checked against the 51-county demo database on 2026-10-05.",
 "buckets": {
